 <!--
-    KaamLink design tokens — single source of truth for color (2026 refresh).
-    Screens reference these tokens (or style classes in Styles.xaml), never raw hex.
-    Rationale: rich indigo/violet brand + warm amber accent on warm "stone" neutrals —
-    moves the product away from the flat teal/blue-gray "ERP" look. Key NAMES are
-    frozen (pages bind to them); only VALUES evolve. Dark-mode palette is introduced
-    together with dark-mode support in a later phase (AppThemeBinding), not piecemeal.
+    KaamLink theme palette — "Clay" (default, light).
+    Spec: docs/ui-redesign/04-claymorphism-theme.md
+
+    This file is a THEME DICTIONARY, not the whole design system:
+      * palette + clay tokens live here (swapped by ThemeService when the user
+        picks another theme);
+      * icon glyphs live in Icons.xaml because they never change with a theme;
+      * typography, spacing and control recipes live in Styles.xaml.
+
+    Rules:
+      * Every key here must also exist in every other theme dictionary
+        (Resources/Themes/*.xaml) — tools/verify-ui-redesign.py fails otherwise,
+        because a missing token shows up as a half-themed screen.
+      * Pages/setters reference these keys through {DynamicResource ...} so a
+        theme switch repaints the live app. Never hard-code a hex in a page.
+      * Soft-clay surfaces use calm tonal fills, explicit component edges, and a
+        restrained cast shadow. Brand action fills retain their gradient. Palette
+        contrast is measured by tools/verify-theme-contrast.py.
 -->
